<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean firms seek 23,000T China cottonseed meal.</title>
<headline>South Korean firms seek 23,000T China cottonseed meal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five South Korean feed milling firms have invited bids for a total of 23,000 tonnes of Chinese cottonseed meal, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said the five included Miwon Co Ltd, Purina Korea Inc and Taihan Sugar Industrial Co Ltd.  </p>
<p>A trader said the buyers were looking for the meal below $150 per tonne, C&amp;F. He said it was $3 to $4 lower than current market prices.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p> AMOUNT (TONNE)	     ARRIVAL		 PORT</p>
<p>    10,000		  January 20	    Inchon</p>
<p>     5,000		  January 20	    Kunsan</p>
<p>     8,000		  March 20		Inchon and Kunsan</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
